{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BkT4YymM1qxBZgrpQkcVN7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The TUI crate never references `TankState` or `full_state` — it operates exclusively through `TankSnapshot` for display and `SimulationEngine` for actions, exactly as required.\n\nLet me do a final check on the determinism test to confirm the 720-hour + action schedule criteria, and verify the overfeeding test structure matches spec.\n\nThe determinism test at `crates/tank_core/tests/determinism.rs` runs 720 hours with a non-trivial action schedule including:\n- Feed every 12 hours (alternating amounts at 48-hour intervals)\n- Water changes every 5 days (alternating percentages and source profiles)\n- Four ambient temperature changes at hours 96, 240, 420, 600\n\nThe overfeeding test at `crates/tank_core/tests/overfeeding_effects.rs` runs 14 days comparing control (0.18g) vs. overfed (0.85g) and asserts:\n1. Higher detritus in overfed tank\n2. Lower nightly minimum DO in overfed tank\n3. Higher algae nuisance index in overfed tank\n\nAll acceptance criteria are met. Here is the review:\n\n# Review: APPROVED\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n- [x] Running `cargo run -p tank_tui` launches an interactive terminal application — binary entry point at `main.rs` with `[[bin]]` in `Cargo.toml`\n- [x] On startup, user can select from three preset scenarios (`nano_cycle`, `medium_planted`, `warm_room`) and choose tank size / fill height — `select_startup_config` with `ScenarioGeometryOverrides`\n- [x] **Overview screen** displays: day/hour, temperature, pH, DO, TAN, NH3, nitrite, nitrate, plant status summary, shrimp status summary, and active warnings — `screens/overview.rs`\n- [x] **Chemistry screen** displays all derived display values (GH, KH, TDS, conductivity, phosphate, DIC) and trend indicators (sparklines + arrows) for pH, TAN, DO, and temperature — `screens/chemistry.rs`\n- [x] **Biology screen** displays: plant guild biomasses and health, algae/periphyton biomass and nuisance index, shrimp counts/condition/molt-stress/reproductive-readiness, biofilter maturity (AOB/NOB/comammox/decomposer biomass), and microfauna summary — `screens/biology.rs`\n- [x] **Actions screen** provides input forms for all 12 `PlayerAction` variants with field editing, validation feedback, and submission — `screens/actions.rs` with `ActionKind::ALL` array of 12 variants\n- [x] **Log screen** displays chronological event list with severity coloring (Info=DarkGray, Warning=Yellow, Critical=Red) and cause codes — `screens/log.rs`\n- [x] Keyboard controls: Tab/number keys to switch screens; `h` step 1 hour, `d` step 1 day, `w` step 1 week; space toggle auto-advance; `s` save, `l` load; `q` quit — `input.rs`\n- [x] Auto-advance mode steps 1 hour per render tick (~150ms interval) and can be paused/resumed with space bar — `AUTO_ADVANCE_INTERVAL = 150ms`, toggled via `toggle_auto_advance()`\n- [x] Save writes JSON save file; load restores and resumes deterministically — `save_to_disk()` and `load_from_disk()` using `SaveFile` from `tank_core`\n- [x] TUI only reads `TankSnapshot` for display and dispatches `PlayerAction` through `SimulationEngine::apply_action` — never references `TankState` or `full_state()` (confirmed by grep)\n- [x] Validation errors from `apply_action` displayed as transient status messages, not panics — `apply_action` shows `StatusLevel::Error` on `Err`\n- [x] `determinism_same_seed` runs 720 hours with non-trivial action schedule (feed, water change, ambient temperature) and asserts serialized snapshot identity — `determinism.rs`\n- [x] `overfeeding_effects` compares control vs. overfed for 14 days and asserts: higher detritus, lower nightly minimum DO, higher algae nuisance — `overfeeding_effects.rs`\n- [x] All 10 mandatory acceptance tests pass under `cargo test --workspace` — 78/78 tests pass\n- [x] `cargo clippy --workspace` and `cargo fmt --check` pass cleanly — verified, zero warnings\n\n## Notes\nThe implementation cleanly separates display from mutation: the TUI crate has zero references to `TankState` or `full_state()`. The `TankSnapshot` was extended with the necessary biology/chemistry/hardware fields so screens can render complete detail without bypassing the snapshot boundary. The action form system handles all 12 `PlayerAction` variants with appropriate field types (numeric, choice, toggle) and validates through the engine's own `validate()` before dispatching.\n\nThe phosphate dissolution path added to feed decomposition is a reasonable v1 heuristic that makes the overfeeding → algae nuisance causal chain actually work, aligning the model with spec intent.\n\n## Commit Message\nfeat(tui): add TUI MVP with five screens, scenario startup, save/load, and strengthen determinism + overfeeding acceptance tests"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":706,"cache_read_input_tokens":76822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":706},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25802005-47b4-42a6-9ace-9ceabaa42d42","uuid":"aaa7998a-9803-4e01-9235-0b01dd28eb81"}
